keiko 1
# B1 (recipe B: a broken pack) — the pack fails to load before the title, so the
# error screen is the only surface, and the dev Monitor opens over it and closes
# back to it.
# Excluded: the load errors' text and the session-log pointer (the observation's
# `error` field has no `expect` form, and the pointer is drawn chrome), the
# player's nonzero startup exit (a normal launch opens a real window the test
# environment cannot run), and the twenty-error cap/overflow fixtures.
#
# The fixture pack itself stays loadable: `--take` loads a pack before it runs
# any case, so a genuinely broken pack cannot reach a case at all. The recipe's
# break is therefore a `fault` header, which deletes the manifest from the
# take's own sandbox copy (spec §7.2), and the take then boots to the error
# screen exactly as a broken launch does.
fault pack-file-missing pack.ron
dev
setting play.text_speed 0

expect surface error
expect control title.new-game absent
press F3
expect monitor open
press Escape
expect monitor closed
expect surface error
